      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T20:27:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that a Binder VMA starting inside a 16KB page breaks the absolute `PAGE_MASK` math: for the first buffer, `start` lands below `vm_start`, so its index wraps far past `pages[]`.\n\nAs far as I can see, though, only an address hint or `MAP_FIXED` gets there. libbinder maps with a NULL address, and since aosp/4312485 `vm_unmapped_area()` aligns those mappings to 16KB in 4KB processes (`p3s_adjust_unmapped_area_info()`).\n\nWould refusing the other mappings in `binder_mmap()` work for you? Then `binder_alloc.c` could keep upstream\u0027s math, and P3S would only add a hook there:\n\n```\n\tif (!vma_starts_at_kernel_page(vma))\n\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n```\n\nwith the helper next to `vma_slice_off()` in `include/linux/p3s/vma.h`:\n\n```\nstatic inline bool vma_starts_at_kernel_page(const struct vm_area_struct *vma)\n{\n\treturn PAGE_ALIGNED_KERNEL(vma-\u003evm_start) \u0026\u0026 !vma_slice_off(vma);\n}\n```\n\nNative VMAs always pass, and the `vm_slice_off` part also covers the offset case in my comment on `binder_install_buffer_pages()`. A misaligned hint would make `mmap()` fail, though; if such mappings need to work, could the three helpers move into a P3S header such as `include/linux/p3s/binder.h` instead?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "a55bca1345dcacbafdc962d5abc851b6f603b918",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
