      "message": "I\u0027m worried this doesn\u0027t skip on kernels without P3S. `personality()` accepts `ADDR_PAGE_SIZE_4KB` on any kernel, so `exec_compat()` always re-execs. On a 16KB kernel without P3S, the `--run` child still has 16KB pages and this check fails. On a 4KB kernel, all five checks pass without exercising P3S (the hint is only misaligned against the hard-coded `NATIVE_PAGE_SIZE`).\n\nCould `run_in_private_binderfs()` skip unless `getpagesize() \u003d\u003d NATIVE_PAGE_SIZE`, as `p3s_compat_main()` from aosp/4396645 does, and the `--run` path call `p3s_require_compat()` before `run_test()`?",
